			(do_not_autoplace no)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
			)
		)
		(property "Note" "B-70 CLOSED 2026-08-23 (FBV2-S2-002). Murata LQW18AN39NG80D, 0603/1608 wire-wound ceramic, 39 nH +/-2% (G), Rdc 0.20 R max, SRF 3000 MHz min, Q 37 min, Irated 1 A. CHECKED AGAINST D-134, NOT LOCKED FROM HEADLINE SPECS: (1) SRF 3000 MHz is 74x the 40.68 MHz third harmonic and 149x the 20.1 MHz EMC corner, so the part is a pure inductor across the whole band of interest; (2) X_L = 3.32 R at 13.56 MHz, which is the reactance D-134 already solved the match against; (3) DCR IS NOT NEGLIGIBLE HERE - 0.20 R max sits in series with R_q = 1.1 R, so worst-case arm resistance is 1.30 R and the network Q falls from 25.3 to about 21.4, roughly -15%. That moves FURTHER INTO the safe, under-driven side D-134 deliberately chose, so it is not a stress condition, but the antenna MUST be tuned on the bench with this exact part fitted. If field strength is short at first article the first lever is R_q 1.1 R -> 0.9 R, NOT a change to 39 nH (D-134 forbids moving L without re-running the whole matching calculation); (4) coil current about 187 mA worst case against a 1 A rating, >5x margin. LCSC C2042966, stock 270 on 2026-08-23. LCSC/JLC library state verified live on 2026-08-23 through the JLCPCB parts API (D-096). Stock is a snapshot, not a guarantee."
			(at 308.61 129.54 0)
			(hide yes)
			(show_name no)
			(do_not_autoplace no)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
			)
		)
