		(uuid "fb044020-e020-4e20-9e20-000000000020")
	)
	(text "J7 BM02B-ACHSS-GAN-ETF, JST ACH, 2 circuits, 1.2 mm, SMT, gold, 2.0 A. It mates the ACHR-02V-S housing, which is the ACH(F) connector already fitted to the antenna cable - so the antenna is REPLACEABLE WITHOUT SOLDERING. JST classes ACH as TOP ENTRY: the socket drops on vertically and the wires leave horizontally. Leave vertical clearance above J7 for mating."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 380.0 104.0 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "fb044021-e021-4e21-9e21-000000000021")
	)
	(text "Antenna: Taoglas FXC.46.52.0075X.B.dg - the B VERSION, REVERSE FERRITE LAYER (SPE-24-8-104-B). 13.56 MHz, 46 mm diameter, 0.3 mm, peel-and-stick 3M adhesive, 75 mm twisted pair 28 AWG, ACH(F). Stack order is ADHESIVE / FLEX ANTENNA / FERRITE, so it bonds ADHESIVE-SIDE to the INNER REAR SHELL and reads OUTWARD through the plastic with the ferrite facing INWARD at the PCB and battery (Taoglas APN-24-8-001). The A version is for bonding onto a PCB or component surface and is NOT the right part here. IT DOES NOT GO ON THE PCB."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 380.0 112.0 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "fb044022-e022-4e22-9e22-000000000022")
	)
	(text "MATCHING BASIS (FBV2-S1-004C, AN5276 Rev 6 workflow): FXC.46.B published La 1.10 uH, Rs 1.50 R, Q 60.37, SRF 395 MHz. wL = 93.72 R at 13.56 MHz. CALCULATED FIRST-BUILD SET, not final tuning: R_q 1R1 per leg -> R_total 3.70 R -> Q 25.3. C_s 300pF per leg (ideal 284pF; 300pF is the E24 neighbour on the SAFE, lower-current side) -> about 68 R differential, 0.13 W, coil current about 187 mA, driver about 60 mA. C_p 1.5nF completes the L-match. EMC: L 39nH with the 1.6nF total shunt gives f_c 20.1 MHz - AN5276 forbids a cut-off between 13 and 14 MHz, and the old 220nH pair sat at 7.6 MHz, BELOW the carrier. RX divider 27pF / 620pF holds RFI at about 1.0 Vpp per side against a 3.0 V regulated rail; the previous 47pF / 220pF would have driven it to about 4.4 Vpp, ABOVE the rail. FINAL VALUES COME FROM A VNA WITH THE REAR SHELL, PCB AND BATTERY IN PLACE."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 380.0 118.0 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "fb044023-e023-4e23-9e23-000000000023")
	)
)
